# 0022 — OpenRouter free models never bill, and nothing secret is sent to OpenRouter (the free-model fallback).
# Status: APPLIED by setup-station.sh.
# Why (2026-11-21): the free-model fallback (docs/FREE-MODELS.md) runs a seat on a free OpenRouter model when every
# subscription entry of its chain cannot run. Free providers may keep or train on prompts, so two rules hold on this
# wire, in the adapter itself (sidecar/providers/openrouter.js), on every request it sends:
#   1. a free model (id ending ':free', a catalog row priced 0 everywhere, or an id on the company's free list, env
#      STARNET_OPENROUTER_FREE_POOL = company/state/free-models.json) is sent with provider.max_price
#      {prompt:0, completion:0, request:0, image:0}, so no endpoint that charges can serve it; it may also carry a
#      `models` list of up to 2 further free ids from that list (OpenRouter fails over within the request; patch 0016's
#      servedModel names the model that answered). STARNET_OPENROUTER_FREE_ONLY=1 puts that zero max price on EVERY
#      request and refuses a model that is not free before anything is sent.
#   2. the finished request body (system, user, assistant and tool messages, tool-call arguments, cache-control parts)
#      goes through sidecar/outbound-scrub.js (a byte-identical copy of the framework's company/tools/lib/outbound-scrub.js):
#      the exact values of every file in STARNET_SCRUB_SECRETS_DIR (the company's secrets/), then every secret format in
#      STARNET_SCRUB_PATTERNS (company/tools/lib/secret-patterns.json), each replaced by [REDACTED:<kind>]; counts per run
#      (never a value) go to the JSON-lines file STARNET_SCRUB_LOG. Neither variable set = as before; set but unreadable =
#      the request is refused, nothing is sent. The factory's existing guard (prompt-scrub.js) still runs first.
# OpenRouter's daily free-model limit is already a non-retryable quota_exhausted (errorClass.js DAILY_FREE_CAP_RE).
# Env (written by scripts/setup-station.sh): STARNET_SCRUB_SECRETS_DIR, STARNET_SCRUB_PATTERNS, STARNET_SCRUB_LOG,
# STARNET_OPENROUTER_FREE_POOL, STARNET_OPENROUTER_FREE_ONLY (1 unless model-policy.json allowed.openrouter.paid is true).
# Test: company/patches/tests/0022.test.js (a stub OpenRouter server on loopback; nothing reaches the internet).
# Apply:  git -C starnet apply --3way company/patches/0022-openrouter-free-scrub.diff ; then restart the station when idle.
# Revert: git -C starnet apply -R company/patches/0022-openrouter-free-scrub.diff ; then restart the station.
